                <pb facs="0352" n="258" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg258"/>

                <head>No. 208.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-02-05"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 5, 1887</date>.
                        (Received March 31.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 58.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Previous dispatches from this legation have
                    informed the Department, of the opening in Seoul, by a number of American
                    missionaries, of schools, an orphanage, a hospital, and of other useful
                    undertakings due to them. In all these they have received the hearty support of
                    this legation.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
